question:
A developer created a Business Rule on the Incident table (before Insert) that loops through all open high-priority incidents and updates the 'assignment_group' on each related Problem record to a specific group. The code works perfectly in the development instance with ~500 incidents but times out consistently in production with 100k+ incidents. Here's the problematic code:

<pre>(function executeRule(current, previous /*null when async*/) {

   var inc = new GlideRecord('incident');
   inc.addQuery('priority', '1');
   inc.addActiveQuery();
   inc.query();
   while(inc.next()) {
      var prob = new GlideRecord('problem');
      prob.addQuery('incident', inc.sys_id);
      prob.query();
      while(prob.next()) {
         prob.assignment_group = 'sys_id_of_group';
         prob.update();
      }
   }

})(current, previous);</pre>

Explain how you'd identify this performance issue, what specific anti-patterns are present, and provide an optimized solution. What ServiceNow best practices would prevent this in the future?
